{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Information Systems for Business Effectiveness"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use when talking about information systems."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about relational database management system in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level.   Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verb + ing, position of not"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The gerund, which is the <strong>\u2013ing</strong> form of a verb, can be used as the subject of a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Gerunds can be used as regular nouns. The gerund is a word that ends in</span> \u2013<strong>ing</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>that is made from a verb. The gerund can be used as the subject of a sentence.<br> Take a look at the following example:<br><br></span><li><strong>Applying</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>information systems to improve the organization's productivity is mandatory.<br><br>A gerund can be affirmative or</span> <strong>negative. </strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>To make the<span> <strong>negative</strong>  form, place <strong>not</strong>  before the \u2013<strong>ing</strong>  subject:<br><br> <li><strong>Not realizing</strong>  about the importance of information systems may lead to negative consequences."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Not being aware of the effect that evolving information systems have on companies might lead to unfavorable situations."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Not knowing how successfully the company is may lead to just getting customer satisfaction, and not customer delight."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "To + verb, position of not"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Some verbs are followed specifically by -ing or <strong>infinitive forms</strong> of the verbs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><i>Management <strong>needs to implement</strong> the appropriate information system in the company.</i><br><br>The negative infinitive is made by placing</span> <strong>not</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>before the</span> <strong>to infinitive.<br><br>Not + To Infinitive</strong><br><br> For example:<br><br><i><li>The manager is determined <strong>not to ignore</strong> the company's needs in terms of information systems.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is advisable not to overlook the importance of protecting this valuable and sensitive information with information assurance systems, due to the susceptibility of misappropriation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Organization managers who happen not to be aware of this may eventually make their companies get behind in the highly competitive technology marketplace."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Information systems as value add for an organization"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The use and development of information systems have changed the rules of competition among organizations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Information systems are implemented as an organizational strategy in order to achieve a company's short-term and long term goals. The organization environment, management style and organization structure within a business may affect how successful the implementation of an information system is going to be.<br/ > The appropriate appliance of information systems can enable an organization to reduce operational costs, improve productivity, create a loyal customer base, etc. thus making it highly competitive and profitable."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rewrite "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "write something again "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Nowadays, technology is rewriting the rules of competition among companies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aware "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " knowing something  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Not being aware of the effect that evolving information systems have on companies might lead to unfavorable situations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "effectiveness "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to succeed at making or doing something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That is why it is necessary for managers to give importance to the contribution of information systems in business effectiveness."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wisely "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " in a way that reflects good judgement "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Organizations need to implement strategies in order to use information systems wisely, so that there is a significant increase in productivity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "customer delight "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "satisfying or pleasing a customer beyond their expectations"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Not knowing how successfully the company is may lead to just getting customer satisfaction, and not customer delight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "get behind "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fail to do something in terms of specific expectations"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Organization managers who happen not to be aware of this may eventually make their companies get behind in the highly competitive technology marketplace."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for extra information about information systems benefits on business.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write some notes and create a comparative chart which shows business before and after information systems implementation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your partners and get some extra knowledge"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for extra information about information systems benefits on business. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a comparative chart to show business before and after information systems implementation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about information system implementation on business."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Nowadays, technology is rewriting the rules of competition among companies. Not being aware of the effect that evolving information systems have on companies might lead to unfavorable situations. That is why it is necessary for managers to give importance to the contribution of information systems in business effectiveness.<br>\nThis rapid evolving development in information systems is mainly due to advances in information technology and computing. However, organizations need to implement strategies in order to use information systems wisely, so that there is a significant increase in productivity.<br><br>"}, {"time": "46500", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Although automation is one of the most common ways that information systems are applied, it is innovation what really makes organizations competitive. In the scenario of performance indicators, not knowing how successfully the company is, may lead to just getting customer satisfaction, and not customer delight. Information systems with marketing analytics capability may provide managers with sufficient customer feedback to develop products or services that go beyond customers' expectations, thus creating a loyal customer base. It is advisable not to overlook the importance of protecting this valuable and sensitive information with information assurance systems, due to the susceptibility of misappropriation. <br><br>"}, {"time": "103000", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>The application of information systems to routine processes such as sales and cash transactions, payrolls, among others will contribute to the desired organizational productivity and effectiveness. The use of video conferencing, email, and other collaboration software also guarantees an effective execution of an organization's projects or tasks.<br>\nOn the whole, information systems have become a priority issue for organizations that are looking for innovative strategies to stand out. Organization managers who happen not to be aware of this, may eventually make their companies get behind in the highly competitive technology marketplace."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le01ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the importance of recognizing information systems contribution in business effectiveness. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explore ideas about innovation opportunities."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss information about systems and organizational productivity."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you think the application of information systems can improve an organization's productivity?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What innovative ways of applying information systems can be implemented in order to make an organization more effective?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "The Importance of Information Systems for Business Effectiveness"}], 